Track 1: Freight-Train To The Dredge
- Story & Context: Old Man Miller discovered a rusted navigational buoy washed up on the riverbank that emitted a high-pitched, harmonic whine whenever the wind hit it just right. He tried to record the sound in his garage, but the buoy's signal began calling out to the heavy ships passing in the mist, sparking a local panic when they started veering off course. The track begins with the buoy’s mournful groan, followed by Miller screaming, "Hold your breath until the hull hits the pier!"
