Track 2: Draft-Depth Calculations
- Story & Context: Elena, the group's lead synth player, spent a week trapped in the Port Authority tower during a record-breaking white-out storm that silenced all comms. She found a ledger detailing the weight of ships that never actually docked, realizing she had been playing the bass frequencies of ghosts to guide them home. She finally confronted the station commander, whispering, "How much weight can a dream hold before the steel ribs finally crack?"
