Track 3: Dock-Rot Vesper
- Story & Context: Long after the industrial harbor was shuttered, the kids of the district would gather at the abandoned slips to hear the "Ship-Song" played by the rising tide through the hollow concrete pillars. It is said that if you stand in the center of the slip long enough, you lose your shadow, left only with the rhythmic thump of the harbor’s heartbeat against your chest. They sing the final rite: "Salt takes the iron, but we take the sound."
